# Screenshots must not contain personal data

Every screenshot saved under `images/docs/` must be free of personal data BEFORE it is
written to the repo. Never commit a screenshot and fix it afterwards.

## What counts as personal data

- Email addresses
- Real names of people
- Account names and account IDs that identify a real account
- Phone numbers, IP addresses, API tokens, any credential

## How to remove it, in this order

1. **Hide it in the page with JavaScript before capturing.** Run this in the browser
   before every screenshot. `visibility: hidden` keeps the layout unchanged:

```javascript
document.querySelectorAll('span, p, div, a, button').forEach(el => {
  if (el.children.length === 0 && /[^@\s]+@[^@\s]+\.[^@\s]+/.test(el.textContent || '')) {
    el.style.visibility = 'hidden';
  }
});
```

   Adapt the selector when the data is an account name, account ID, or phone number
   rather than an email. Target the specific element and hide or replace its text.

2. **Frame the shot so the data is outside it.** Crop to the region that shows the
   documented UI and leave the header, avatar menu, or account bar out of the frame
   when they are not the subject.

3. **Replace the text with a placeholder** (for example `user@example.com`,
   `my-account`, `ID 0001`) when the element itself is what the screenshot documents
   and cannot be hidden or cropped out. A blurred or pixelated real value is acceptable
   only when replacement is impossible.

## Check before saving

Read the captured image back and scan it for emails, real names, and real account
identifiers. If any remain, retake the screenshot. Do not rely on a later manual edit.
